<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Newfoundland Regiment</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Newfoundland Regiment</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> Regiment is an infantry regiment, now part of the Canadian Army reserve, raised as the Newfoundland Regiment in 1914 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Gallipoli</a> and on the Western Front and was nearly destroyed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beaumont-hamel">Beaumont-Hamel</a> on 1 July 1916. It was granted the title 'Royal' in 1917 for its service, a rare honour in wartime.</p></div>
